    Add option to reset the SSNR noise estimation fcn
       Selecting R in the SSNR dropdown will reset the SSNR noise estimation
       function for either the main receiver or the sub receiver.
   
    Say what Dit Mem % means on a hover
       The box is a bare number under a four-character title, and neither says
       what the percentage is a percentage of.
       
       The text joins the group box's title, the setting name and the default
       in memory_delay_percent_setting, the other strings this one box is
       built out of.
       
       On the frame as well as the box, so the title answers to a hover too --
       it is the title that names what this is. WA_Hover on both for the
       reason Togglebutton sets it: without it Qt stops generating hover
       events on Windows once connected to a K4.
   
    Let a dropdownbutton carry a tooltip
       tooltip was a Togglebutton selection's option and nothing else, so a
       dropdownbutton given one was refused outright by validate_options.
       
       One for the whole control rather than one per selection, which is where
       the difference from Togglebutton is: a toggle's selections are what it
       says, so each carries its own text and configure() swaps them as the
       button changes; a dropdown's selections set a value, and what wants
       explaining is the control they set it on, which does not change.
       
       Set on the frame as well as the box so the label answers to a hover
       too. Where the item has a label that frame is the group box the label
       titles, and both come up -- checked against a labelled dropdown, where
       the Power group box and its box both carry it. Where it has none the
       frame is a plain widget wrapping the box, and the box alone shows it.
       
       WA_Hover on both for the same reason Togglebutton sets it: without it
       Qt stops generating hover events on Windows once connected to a K4.
   
    Remove the dah memory delay setting
       The Dah Mem % box is gone; Dit Mem % stays. Nothing about the keying
       changes: the dah setting defaulted to 0 and the two tests it gated were
       "later than the element" plus a zero, which is what they say outright
       now. All seven kept summaries in keying_simulations are byte identical,
       and the squeeze sweep passes at 20, 30, 40 and 50 WPM.
       
       With one side left there is nothing for the side parameter to choose
       between, so it goes too: memory_delay_percent_settings was a dict keyed
       by side and is now the one tuple, the frame and entry were dicts and are
       now the widgets themselves, and the builder, the change handler and the
