       A group's columns are only as wide as the items in them, so a row of
       items sits bunched wherever the row's own alignment puts it however
       much room it has. The antenna row -- Main Rx, Tx and Sub Rx, each a
       label and a dropdown -- was centred, and ran 49..428 across a page
       whose VFO panels run 2..476: floating in the middle rather than
       standing under the panels it belongs to. Padding could not fix it.
       Widening the gaps grows the row symmetrically, so it reaches one edge
       only by overshooting the other, and any fixed figure is wrong at a
       different width.
       
       item: spacer is an empty grid cell that takes the width its row has
       spare. It is not a Widget: no label, no leading, no padding, nothing to
       show. An optional weight sets its share where two in a row should not
       come out the same.
       
