    Version 1.6.16.34

    Specify low-latency wanted for sound device

    Port audio I/O from pyaudio to sounddevice for real WASAPI exclusive mode
       Neither pyaudio nor PyAudioWPatch wrap a WASAPI-specific stream-info
       struct, so exclusive mode could never actually be requested through
       them. sounddevice's WasapiSettings(exclusive=True) is genuine and
       PortAudio honors it -- confirmed by forcing it against this machine's
       ALSA device and getting a real PaErrorCode -9984 (incompatible host
       API specific stream info), caught by the same retry-then-fall-back-
       to-shared-mode logic used before.
       
       Device enumeration, output_loop/input_loop's stream open+retry, and
       output_stream_callback are all rewritten onto sounddevice's API
       (RawOutputStream/RawInputStream, module-level query/check functions
       instead of a PyAudio() session object, writing into a mutable outdata
       buffer instead of returning (data, flag)). Verified end-to-end against
       real ALSA/PulseAudio devices in a local venv: device enumeration,
       real audio flowing through both streams, the exclusive/shared fallback
       path, and full Audio.close() shutdown all work without mocks.
       
       Requires `pip install sounddevice`; pyaudio is no longer imported.
   
    Double output frames_per_buffer to 4
       We were getting dropouts on Windows with frames_per_buffer == 2.
   
