    Version 1.6.16.26

    keyer: Send sidetone with computed elements

    Fix Windows hang closing main window while CW window is open
       Reorders clean_up() so CW/Macros close before the K4 server is
       disconnected rather than after -- CW.close() can still send a real
       command (stop_sending()'s 'KY @;') if text was actively being sent,
       and doing that after the server was already marked disconnected
       triggered a spurious "not connected" warning -- and flushes their
       top_level.deleteLater() to actually run immediately rather than
       leaving it pending when quit() stops the event loop right after.
   
    Testing with shorter Morse elements

    Suppress benign QThreadStorage warning on panadapter window close
       Closing a panadapter window directly (not via the parent) leaves its
       reader thread parked in a blocking stdin read when os._exit() runs
       (see panadapter_child_main's own comment on why that's unavoidable),
       so Qt's per-thread teardown for that thread happens out of order.
       Filters just that one message via a global Qt message handler rather
       than the other messages passing through unchanged.
   
    Fix morse code weighting

    Rework panadapter click-tune/nudge granularity, hide auto-range button
       - Click-to-tune now rounds to an explicit per-plot Hz granularity
         (mini-pan 1 Hz, trace 100 Hz, waterfall 1 kHz) instead of a khz/not
         flag, generalizing request_tune/on_tune_requested.
       - Arrow-key/wheel nudge sizes bumped a decade coarser per area
         (mini-pan 10 Hz, trace 100 Hz, waterfall 1 kHz, button area 1 Hz),
         and now do nothing at all over the trace/waterfall splitter handle
         or the window's own margins, rather than falling back to some
         default rate. The button-area rate covers the whole upper-right
         row (controls_frame plus the stretch beside it), not just the
         controls widget itself.
       - Hide pyqtgraph's built-in auto-range ('A') button on all three
         plots -- it only ever showed on hover and would fight the app's
         own manual axis control if clicked.
   
    Add Autospot button to each panadapter, enabled only in CW/CW-R
       Placed on row one after Freeze; sends SP3;/SP$3; (main/sub) through
       the same parent-relay channel as Center. Visibility tracks the
       receiver's own MD;/MD$; mode independently per window.
   
    Version 1.6.16.25

    Add Scale combobox to panadapters, bound to #SCL;
       Placed to the left of Span, listing every 5th value in the 10-150
       range with a dynamic extra item for whatever in-between value the
       radio last reported -- same mechanism Span already uses, since #SCL
       isn't actually restricted to multiples of 5.
   
    Lock down Span combobox and fix display for out-of-list values
       Span is now a plain non-editable, non-focusable dropdown like FPS/Fixed
       Tune: Up/Down and the mouse wheel no longer step it (they fall through
       to the normal window-wide VFO nudge instead), and it can't take
       keyboard focus. Removed the now-dead SteppedComboBox/typing/validator
       wiring and _PanControlFilter's special-case carve-outs for it.
       
       Fixed a resulting display bug: since the combobox is no longer
       editable, setCurrentText() silently does nothing for a #SPN;/#SPN$;
       value that isn't one of the 7 preset choices, leaving the display
       stuck on a stale value. _set_span_combobox_khz now adds (and replaces,
       never accumulates) a dynamic item for any such value so it's always
       reflected accurately.
   
    Vary panadapter arrow-key/wheel nudge size by cursor position
       Mini-pan nudges by 1 Hz, trace by 10 Hz, waterfall by 100 Hz, and
       anywhere else in the panadapter window by 1 kHz (previously a no-op).
       Also drops the now-unreachable None handling in the key/wheel handlers
       since _nudge_size_hz always returns a size now.
   
    Minimize vertical padding in all combobox popups
       QSS's ::item padding/min-height has no effect on a combobox popup's
       actual row height on this app's styles -- confirmed against real
       measurements, not just theory. Replaced with a small item delegate
       (_TightComboBoxDelegate/qt_tighten_combobox_popup) that overrides
       sizeHint() directly, setting each row to exactly the font's own line
       height with nothing added, applied at every combobox construction site
       (the module-level readonly combobox helper, DropdownWidget, Equalizers,
       the panadapter's Span/FPS/Fixed Tune comboboxes, and the generic
       Dropdown_Widget).
   
    Version 1.6.16.24

    Add Fixed Tune combobox to the panadapter
       Adds a DDC Fixed Tune Mode selector (Track/Fixed1/Fixed2/Slide1/
       Slide2/Static, values 5/0/1/2/4/3) between Center and Freeze,
       bidirectionally connected to #FXA;/#FXT;. Picking a 0-4 item sets that
       #FXA mode and sends #FXT1;; picking Track sends #FXT0; alone. #FXT0;
       always selects Track; #FXT1; selects whichever item matches the
       current #FXA value, and a later #FXA change while already fixed keeps
       the display in sync too. Both are shared (no per-receiver $ variant),
       same as FPS/#FRZ.
   
    Add Freeze/Unfreeze button to the panadapter
       Adds a two-valued toggle to the right of Center, bidirectionally
       connected to #FRZ; (panadapter/waterfall freeze, shared with no
       per-receiver $ variant). Shows "Freeze" while running and "Unfreeze"
       while frozen; a local click sends #PANFRZ to the parent, which issues
       #FRZ0;/#FRZ1; to the radio, and any #FRZ; response updates every open
       window's button, same as FPS.
   
    Add FPS combobox to the panadapter
       Adds an FPS selector (values 1-30, per the K4 Programmer's Reference'
       #FPSnn; range) to the right of the Span combobox. Bidirectionally
       connected to #FPS;: a local selection sends #PANFPS to the parent,
       which issues #FPS{nn}; to the radio, and any #FPS; response -- from
       this window, another window, or the radio itself -- updates every open
       panadapter's combobox, since #FPS is shared with no per-receiver ($)
       variant.
   
    Show both VFO A/B frequency lines on both panadapters
       Replace each panadapter's single "own receiver" frequency marker with
       two: VFO A (main receiver, blue) and VFO B (sub receiver, green), shown
       on both the main and sub panadapter windows regardless of which
       receiver the window belongs to -- FA/FB are already relayed to every
       open panadapter subprocess, so both frequencies are available in each.
       Extended onto the waterfall as well as the trace.
   
    Fix window position drift on restart
       Every restored window (main, CW, Panadapter, Macros) positioned itself
       via move()/resize() before its first show(). The window manager only
       attaches its decoration frame once a window is actually mapped, and
       that reparenting happens asynchronously after show() returns -- so the
       pre-show move() request lands before the frame exists, and the WM ends
       up placing the saved position as the frame's top-left instead of the
       content's, drifting the visible content by the title bar/border size
       on every restart. Fixed by re-applying the saved position once more,
       deferred via QTimer.singleShot(0, ...) so it runs after the WM's
       reparenting has actually landed rather than racing it.
   
    Version 1.6.16.22

    Split Autospot into separate Main/Sub buttons
       Relabel the CW page's single cycling Autospot toggle as "Main" and add
       a matching "Sub" button, both inside an "Autospot" group box. Both are
       now plain one-shot QPushButtons (SP3;/SP$3;) rather than a state-cycling
       ToggleWidget, since a manual spot request doesn't have a notion of
       on/off state to cycle through.
   
    Trigger panadapter auto-Ref on antenna, center-frequency, and sub RX on/off
       Mode changes no longer reset Ref (too noisy, not meaningful). Antenna
       changes now debounce through schedule_ref_reset like span, since the
       PAN stream needs a moment to settle to the new antenna's noise floor;
       this also covers a receiver parked on AR/AR$ "RX USES TX ANT" whose
       antenna actually changes via AN instead. Genuine panadapter re-center
       (not ordinary VFO tuning) triggers via push_frame's center_hz. Turning
       the sub receiver on/off (SB) now triggers an auto-Ref on the sub
       panadapter only.
   
    Drain the audio output queue before sending sidetone.

    Version 1.6.16.21

    Fix RF Gain buttons not cycling through all values
       DropdownWidget.set_value() only sent the CAT command and waited
       entirely on the radio's echo to move the displayed value -- for RF
       Gain, that echo wasn't reliably visible, making Up/Down/wheel stepping
       look stuck. Now updates the display immediately, reusing the widget's
       own unexpectedresponse formatting so it matches what the eventual real
       response would show. Applies to any continuous-stepping dropdown
       (evalincrement), not just RF Gain.
       
       Also fixes RF Gain's outgoing command format: {value:+03d} produced
       "RG+00;" at the top of the range, which the K4 doesn't accept (it only
       ever uses a leading '-', per RG$-nn; in the protocol reference) --
       switched to always emit the minus sign.
   
    Make mouse wheel step continuous-range dropdowns like BW
       DropdownWidget comboboxes with evalincrement (BW and similar) already
       let Up/Down step through the full continuous range rather than just
       the enumerated selections; the mouse wheel now does the same, one
       on_increment step per notch, instead of cycling only the enumerated
       items.
   
    Add panadapter Span combobox, fix #SPN$ parsing bug
       Adds a Span combobox to each panadapter window (preset list plus
       editable/steppable entry from 6-368 kHz), bidirectionally synced with
       the K4's #SPN;/#SPN$; span, placed to the right of the mini-pan below
       Ref/Center. Changing the span resets the Ref-captured trace bottom,
       the same as clicking Ref, with a 1-second delay before the actual
       capture since the K4's PAN stream needs a moment to settle at the new
       span -- capturing immediately just re-averages stale, pre-change data.
       
       Also fixes a long-standing bug in cmd_base(): '#SPN$' was missing from
       k4_long_cmd_bases['#S'], so every '#SPN$...' (sub receiver) response
       was misparsed as '#SPN' (main) throughout the app, not just in this
       new feature -- corrupting the sub receiver's own span tracking and its
       Ref auto-reset.
   
