    Set pixel-independent slider width

    Panadapter: sync Main/Sub tab's Pan togglebutton to the window's actual state
       WPAN!/WPAN$! are purely local directives (see directive()), never
       real K4 responses, so main-pan-togglebutton/sub-pan-togglebutton --
       which track state by subscribing to those as if they were -- had no
       way to learn the panadapter window changed state by any means other
       than a click on the button itself.
       
       open_window()/on_exited() are the two paths every open and close
       funnels through respectively (a user's click, restore_open_windows()
       at startup, the window's own close button, or a parent-initiated
       close), so each now calls update_k4_parameter() with a synthetic
       WPAN!/WPAN$! response -- the same mechanism a real CAT parameter
       update uses -- to sync the togglebutton to "On" or "Off". For the
       click-driven path this is a harmless re-affirmation of what the
       button's own local index-advance already set.
       
