    Panadapter: add a Center button; style it and Ref black-on-white
       Center sends the K4's FC;/FC$; ("Center Panadapter for target VFO",
       per the Programmer's Reference) for the window's receiver, re-centering
       the radio's own PAN stream on the current VFO. There's no way to do
       this from software alone the way click-to-tune moves the VFO instead:
       the trace's displayed frequencies come from the PAN stream's own
       center_hz (see push_frame), not from the VFO, so only the radio itself
       can move it. Wired the same way as click-to-tune -- child writes
       #PANCENTER to stdout, monitor_loop emits a new centered signal on that
       line, on_center_requested sends the CAT command -- placed right after
       Ref in the row already built to hold more buttons there.
       
       Both buttons switch from white-on-black to black-on-white.
       
