    Version 1.6.16.8

    Improve keyer inter-character space insertion
       If, after an dit or dah has been sent, no paddle has been pressed
       for 1/2 of an inter-character interval, currently 3 dit lengths,
       we wait an inter-charcter interval since the last dit or daw was
       sent.
   
    Fix stuck CW/VOX delay sliders
       Their evalincrement is negative (-.01), a leftover tk.Scale
       convention from before the Qt port. SliderWidget._set_range() divides
       the slider's low/high bounds by the increment to get QSlider's
       integer step range; with a negative increment that flips the
       low/high inequality, so setMaximum() ends up less than the just-set
       setMinimum() and Qt silently clamps the range to a single value --
       the slider looks normal but can't move. Direction is already handled
       separately via from_/to order and setInvertedAppearance/
       setInvertedControls, so take abs() of the increment wherever it's
       used to convert between the real value and QSlider's steps.
       
       Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
   
    Version 1.6.16.7

    Run the panadapter in a subprocess to stop audio dropouts
       pyqtgraph repaints hold the GIL on the main thread for ~5-20 mS, well
       past the audio output path's ~8 mS tolerance (frames_per_buffer=2,
       kept deliberately shallow for low transmit/tuning delay -- deepening
       the output queue doesn't help either, since the thread that would
       drain it is blocked by the same GIL). A separate process has its own
       GIL, so its repaints can't touch the audio threads at all; measured
       p99 main-thread stall time drops from ~6-9 mS to ~0.2-0.4 mS.
       
       The parent (PanadapterProcess) spawns 'k4companion --panadapter RX'
       and forwards PAN/MINI-PAN payloads and #SPN/#FPS responses over a
       length-framed stdin pipe; the child only reports back its final
       window geometry. Persisted "was open"/geometry state and the
       directive-driven open/close flow are otherwise unchanged.
       
       Also fixes a waterfall rendering regression from the axis-caching
       commit: setRect() must run after the first setImage(), not before --
       pyqtgraph silently drops a rect set before an ImageItem has any image
       data, which left the waterfall's Y-axis auto-ranging against a
       meaningless bounding rect and squeezed the whole scrolling history
       into a handful of banded rows.
       
       Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
   
    Version 1.6.16.6

    Restore audio output buffer length to 2
       THis minimizes audio delay when changing frequency or going into
       transmit mode. Currently, expect audio dropouts when displaying
       the panadapter.
   
    Fix width of dropdown options list

    Cache panadapter axis state to reduce main-thread time per PAN frame
       setXRange/tick-label updates/waterfall setRect only depend on center
       frequency, span, bin count, and waterfall row count, so skip them on
       frames where none of those changed (the common case: the radio sits
       on one frequency). That work cascades through the waterfall's XLink
       into axis label re-rendering every frame, and running it while holding
       the GIL was starving the audio output thread into dropouts.
       
