    Add a workflow to build K4 Companion.app for macOS
       Run by hand, from the Actions tab or with gh workflow run
       build-macos.yml --ref <branch>. On an Apple Silicon and an Intel
       runner, it installs Opus with Homebrew, copies the configuration
       into k4companion.py as ./run does, builds K4 Companion.app from
       tools/k4companion.spec, and keeps it in a .dmg with the run.
       
       The spec's macOS branch bundles Homebrew's libopus.dylib, gives the
       app the microphone usage text macOS asks for before transmit audio
       can open the microphone, turns App Nap off, takes its version from
       the configuration, and leaves out Qt's PDF framework. The app is
       unsigned, so Gatekeeper stops it until it is first opened with
       Control-click, Open.
   
    Add a workflow to build the Windows programs and installer
       Run by hand, from the Actions tab or with gh workflow run
       build-windows.yml --ref <branch>. On a Windows runner with Python
       3.14, it copies example_config_files/k4companion.yaml into
       k4companion.py as ./run does, builds k4companion.exe and
       k4companion-debug.exe with PyInstaller, opus.dll bundled in each,
       builds the installer with tools/k4companion.nsi, and keeps all three
       with the run.
   
