v1.5.1:
    Support cmds that don't directly set a value
       For examples, commands that normally directly set an integer value,
       but can take a special character like +, -, /, ^, >, or ~ to instead
       adjust the current value.
   
    Permit additional characters in macro commands
       We make the following characters permissible: #){}\\&^~`[]|<>:"'
       This should include all printable characters in ASCII.
       Note that & is permitted only if there is an earlier & in the string
       separating the displayed label from the macro command.
   
